     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Thank you for your suggestion.<div><br></div><div>I have done the following for my specific application.</div><div><br></div><div>I have replaced:</div><div><br></div><div>includeCSS(&quot;www/styles.css&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div>with:</div><div><br></div><div><div><div>    tagList(</div><div>      tags$p(</div><div>        tags$style(&quot;.bg-danger {</div><div>                          background-color: #f2dede;</div><div>                        }</div><div>                        </div><div>                        .bg-success {</div><div>                          background-color: #dff0d8;</div><div>                        }&quot;</div><div>                  )</div><div>      )</div><div>    ),</div></div><div><br></div><div>I am getting the same result.  It works in RStudio on the desktop, but not from the Shiny Server hosted on RedHat.</div><div><br></div><div>Basic problem is rstudio picks up the formatting and the shiny server is converting the formatting to text for display (see images below)</div><div><br></div><div>Question:  The way I am accomplishing the formating is by putting the format in the dataframe being displayed, specifically, my code does the following to create the &quot;display version&quot; of the data:</div><div><br></div><div><div>for (c in 2:8) {</div><div>  </div><div>  out[,c] &lt;- ifelse(<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792399930565000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1dE9VzcyBAupwwmNxA5ODj\">is.na</a>(out[,c]), &quot;&lt;p class=&#39;bg-danger&#39;&gt; FALSE &lt;/p&gt;&quot;, &quot;&lt;p class=&#39;bg-success&#39;&gt; TRUE &lt;/p&gt;&quot;)</div><div>  </div><div>  </div><div>}</div></div><div><br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh6.googleusercontent.com/-4YXmfdk33wI/VP3ReqeyodI/AAAAAAAABDM/SFMMzKbZ7qA/s1600/from_Rstudio.png\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh6.googleusercontent.com/-4YXmfdk33wI/VP3ReqeyodI/AAAAAAAABDM/SFMMzKbZ7qA/s1600/from_Rstudio.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792399930565000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3L_4rjxW1tN9Cg1Imvl49z\"><img src=\"https://lh6.googleusercontent.com/-4YXmfdk33wI/VP3ReqeyodI/AAAAAAAABDM/SFMMzKbZ7qA/s320/from_Rstudio.png\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"180\"></a></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><br></p><div>From Shiny Server:</div><div><br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-BeDiOBCFpfA/VP3SVYu8HYI/AAAAAAAABDU/HnAr4ilaIZM/s1600/from_Shiny_server.png\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-BeDiOBCFpfA/VP3SVYu8HYI/AAAAAAAABDU/HnAr4ilaIZM/s1600/from_Shiny_server.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792399930565000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3-Eege95MPiF8OmD6ra4Wg\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-BeDiOBCFpfA/VP3SVYu8HYI/AAAAAAAABDU/HnAr4ilaIZM/s320/from_Shiny_server.png\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"180\"></a></p><div>Any further suggestions on method would be greatly appreciated.</div><div><br></div><div>Stephen...</div></div></div>"
